{#
/**
 * @file
 * Search filter section wrapper. The actual form markup is unchanged
 * and still lives in the reusable components/search-form.html.twig —
 * see that file's header comment for the full field <-> View filter
 * identifier map. Nothing about the form itself (names, ids, submit
 * behavior) is touched here.
 *
 * ADDED for the sticky/collapsible filter behavior (theme.js,
 * "suchauftragStickyFilter" behavior):
 *
 *   - [data-search-filter-sentinel]: a static, zero-height marker that
 *     never moves. theme.js observes it with an IntersectionObserver;
 *     when it scrolls out of view below the header, the section gets
 *     `.is-stuck`. It exists purely so the observer has something
 *     fixed to watch — observing the form itself would break once the
 *     form starts being repositioned.
 *
 *   - [data-search-filter-spacer]: hidden by default. Once `.is-stuck`
 *     is active, theme.js gives this the exact height of whichever
 *     element just became `position:fixed` (the full form on desktop/
 *     tablet, or the compact bar on mobile) so the page content below
 *     never jumps.
 *
 *   - [data-search-filter-bar]: wraps the existing search-form include
 *     only so it can be pinned as a single full-width strip the same
 *     way `.header` already pins itself (see components.css) — this
 *     wrapper carries no visual styling of its own outside `.is-stuck`.
 *
 *   - [data-sticky-bar]: NEW compact "Filter ändern" bar, hidden by
 *     default and only ever shown on mobile once `.is-stuck` is
 *     active (see the ≤780px rules in responsive.css). Clicking it
 *     toggles `.is-expanded` on the section, which reveals the exact
 *     same form (never a duplicate) as a panel underneath it.
 *
 * Desktop/tablet (>780px) ignore `.is-expanded` entirely and always
 * show the full form once stuck — see the "Sticky search filter"
 * rules in components.css. Nothing about the non-stuck, non-mobile
 * appearance changes.
 */
#}
<section class="search-filter" data-search-filter aria-label="Suchaufträge filtern">
  <div class="search-filter__sentinel" data-search-filter-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="search-filter__spacer" data-search-filter-spacer aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="search-filter__bar" data-search-filter-bar>
    <div class="container">
      {% include '@suchauftrag_theme/templates/components/search-form.html.twig' %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {# Compact bar — mobile only, see responsive.css. Summary text is
     filled in and kept in sync by theme.js from the (single) form's
     current values; it is intentionally empty here since there is no
     good static default without duplicating the field labels. #}
  <div class="search-filter__sticky-bar" data-sticky-bar>
    <div class="container search-filter__sticky-bar-inner">
      <button type="button"
              class="search-filter__sticky-toggle"
              data-sticky-toggle
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="search-filter-form">
        <span class="search-filter__sticky-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <path d="M4 6h16M7 12h10M10 18h4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="search-filter__sticky-label">Filter ändern</span>
        <span class="search-filter__sticky-summary" data-filter-summary></span>
        <svg class="search-filter__sticky-chevron" data-sticky-chevron width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
